course: dictionary
lesson: 8118
title: Repatriation: sending home
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Repatriation is a long word, but it is built from two parts you can use. «Re» means back, and «patria» is Latin for homeland. So repatriation means sending or bringing something back to its own country. «Returning objects to the country they came from is called repatriation.»
explain: Use the clues in the sentence. Returning, objects and came from all point the same way: home. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "Returning objects to the country they came from is called sending them back home." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Repatriation can be about people as well as objects. It can mean helping someone return to their own country, or bringing home the body of someone who died abroad. Read the words around it to see which kind of repatriation the text means.
fact: Repatriation is a noun. It means sending or bringing someone or something back to its own country.
fact: Repatriation can mean returning objects, such as money or museum objects, to the country they came from.
fact: In the news, repatriation is often about refugees, prisoners of war or citizens being brought home.
fact: Repatriation can be kind, like bringing someone home, or hard, like sending people back who do not want to go.
fact: The word is built from «re» (back) and «patria» (homeland, from Latin).
exercise: «Returning objects to the country they came from is called repatriation.» What does repatriation mean? | *Sending or bringing something back to its own country | Making a copy of an old object | Moving house within the same town | Taking a holiday abroad
exercise: A museum sends a carved statue back to the country where it was made. Which word fits best? | *Repatriation | Imagination | Excavation | Decoration
exercise: Repatriation is built from «re» and «patria». What does «re» suggest here? | Away from | Under | *Back | Above
test: Which is an example of repatriation? | A family moves to a new house down the road | A girl plays in the park with her friends | *A flight brings prisoners of war back to their home country
test: Which word means sending objects back to the country they came from? | Celebration | *Repatriation | Vacation | Imitation
exam: «The museum agreed to the repatriation of the carved figures.» What is the museum agreeing to? | *Sending the figures back to the country they came from | Making a copy of the figures | Selling the figures in a shop | Keeping the figures forever
